  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6f28a9b2-0db7-4870-a1fb-32fb31f7f7ef",
    "name": "Requests Portal API",
    "description": "**`GET /requests`**  \n  \nReturns all document requests in the system, regardless of status. Response is wrapped in the standard `{ success, data, timestamp }` shape.\n\n**`GET /requests/:id`**  \n  \nReturns a single document request by its id, including the related client. Returns a 404 if no request exists with that id.\n\n**`POST /requests`**  \n  \nCreates a new document request. Requires `title` (string), `clientId` (number, must correspond to an existing client), and optionally `description` (string). Returns a 404 if `clientId` doesn't match a real client. New requests always start with status `pending`.\n\n**`POST /requests/:id/upload`**  \n  \nAllows a client to submit a document against an existing request. Requires `multipart/form-data` with a file under the field name `file`. Accepted types: JPG, JPEG, PNG, PDF. Max file size: 5MB. On success, the request's status automatically transitions to `reviewing` and the file path is saved. Uploading is blocked if the request is already `approved` or `rejected`.\n\n**`PATCH /requests/review/:id`**  \n  \nAllows an accountant to approve or reject a request that is currently in `reviewing` status. Requires `status` (`approved` or `rejected`). If rejecting, `rejectionReason` should be provided. Approving clears any previous rejection reason. Returns a 400 if the request isn't currently in `reviewing` status.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "52406562",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/52406562-6f28a9b2-0db7-4870-a1fb-32fb31f7f7ef?source=collection_link"
  },
